      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "After being platted in 1891, Magnolia officially incorporated as a town in 1894, marking its first formal municipal status.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnolia%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Paul Railway expanded in 1884 and opened a new station in 1886, turning Magnolia into a grain shipping hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/magnolia_minnesota",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Magnolia exhibits a humid continental climate (Köppen Dfa), featuring pronounced seasonal variations with frigid winters and warm summers influenced by its location in the Great Plains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/magnolia_minnesota",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Southwestern Minnesota Plains expose Magnolia to frequent thunderstorms and a moderate tornado risk each spring and summer, part of Tornado Alley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/magnolia_minnesota",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
